            <ArticleTitle>A survey of headache in Parkinson's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are few reports on the prevalence of headache in Parkinson's disease (PD). In the present study, 223 chronic PD sufferers and 291 controls are surveyed by a headache questionnaire. There is no significant difference in the total prevalence of headache in sex and age-matched patients and controls. However, male patients with PD have a higher prevalence of moderate to severe migraine than the control population.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
